 "date": "2026-10-27",
 "purpose": "Line layers for the \"drawn, then built\" arrival on the detail pages (project-motion-arrival.js): one transparent layer per story step, registered on each project's frame-0 cover. case-study.html and project-3d.html run the same arrival on the same cover in the same stage box; a live model (the 3D page, steering's case study) waits behind it and then swaps in as with ?arrival=off. Steering has had its layers since 2026-10-29. No page loads drafting-arrival-20261027.js any more, and it left the site on 2026-11-04: releases/drawn-then-built-20261027/detail-arrival/harness/drafting-arrival-20261027.js still holds the line pass and story orders the layers are rendered with.",
 "renderer": "Three.js r185 with the working-tree studio-inspector.js (rendering unchanged from e42a05b4; it only records merged source parts). Each project is loaded as tools/white-studio/export.js loads a cover (900x600 selection canvas, source camera reset, progress 0; AURA with its aura-reframe-20261022 framing), then the cover camera renders the prepass and line pass of drafting-arrival-20261027.js (same shaders, same story orders ORDERS, same 30-degree folds) at 3600x2400 with paper and ghost removed.",
 "method": "Outlines at part or depth changes #111316, folds #505b66. Premultiplied box-filtered to 1800 and 900 px wide, lossless WebP, transparent background. No pixel of a cover is read to draw the lines; the cover is only used to check registration. Plain parts (ansysCfd flow paths and tracers) are never lined; scientific colours are untouched.",
 "registration": "The harness re-renders each 1800 px cover with the same camera; mean absolute difference to the published poster (lossy WebP) 0.08-0.74 levels, p99 2-16 (per project below). The largest (ansysCfd) is the lossy encoding of its 1 px flow lines and pressure texture, not an offset: no edge is doubled.",
 "layout": "<key>.<tag>/<step>-<width>.webp; tag = first 10 hex of the SHA256 over all of a project's layers. Immutable.",
 "evidence": "releases/drawn-then-built-20261027/detail-arrival/ (harness/layers.js, harness/pack_layers.py, layers-preview/, layers-summary.json); steering (2026-10-29): releases/drawn-then-built-20261027/verify/fix-detail-r2/ (layers-harness/, a copy of that harness on another port; layers-preview/, layers-summary.json)",
